WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.929
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.929 --> 00:00:05.612
which takes about sixty-five
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.612 --> 00:00:09.199
You'll describe a blueprint, an
agent identity and a sponsor,

4
00:00:09.199 --> 00:00:12.200
and why the blueprint is
the credential boundary.

5
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.978
You'll explain decision D N P six as data,

6
00:00:14.978 --> 00:00:18.450
and what the code does in
a cloud without Agent I D.

7
00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.964
You'll run the A I identity
check and read its findings,

8
00:00:21.964 --> 00:00:24.200
including the top-priority drift.

9
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.841
You'll explain the
ten-business-day sponsor rule,

10
00:00:26.841 --> 00:00:28.888
and what happens to an orphaned agent.

11
00:00:28.888 --> 00:00:33.179
And you'll show that the agent
Conditional Access plan is report-only,

12
00:00:33.179 --> 00:00:35.287
and runs only by its approved hash.

13
00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:40.650
Before you start, finish Module 2, because
the lab reads Chapter 2's ownership run,

14
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.780
and Module 6, on Conditional
Access for workload identities.
